From: sie-mcp web <web@sie-mcp.local>
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: chain TCI TBs via goto_tb, account icount2 per TB
 inside the interpreter

The emscripten build disabled TB chaining: tcg_out_goto_tb() emitted
exit_tb so that every TB boundary returned through cpu_exec (the icount2
accounting ran per executed TB in cpu_tb_exec, patches 0002/0004).  The
firmware's branchy code averages ~5.6 insns/TB (~10M TB/s at 5M insns/s),
so the per-boundary round trip - interpreter exit, wasm_exit_account,
cpu_loop_exec_tb, cpu_exec_loop iteration, interrupt check, TB lookup,
re-entry - dominated the profile: cpu_exec_loop 9.3% + cpu_tb_exec 2.6%
+ tb lookup ~2.9% of the vCPU worker's self time (tools/wprof2.mjs).

Chain TBs again and move the clock into the interpreter:

- tcg/tci: tcg_out_goto_tb() emits the stock goto_tb chain jump again;
  tcg_out_tb_start() emits a new INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr header op (opcode
  appended after tci_qemu_st_rrr, numbering-compatible) carrying the
  TB's guest-insn count in its 20-bit immediate.
- tcg/tci.c: the header runs at EVERY TB entry - cpu_tb_exec call,
  goto_tb chain target, goto_ptr target - and advances the icount2
  clock (icount2_advance) + diagnostics (wasm_tb_account) by the TB's
  icount.  The clock stays strictly instruction-proportional while
  chained; interrupt checks are unaffected (gen_tb_start's icount_decr
  brcond runs at each TB start, chained or not).
- cpu_tb_exec: the per-TB post-execution accounting
  (wasm_tb_account + icount2_advance(wasm_io_account_rest())) is gone;
  the interpreter owns the accounting.
- cputlb io_prepare: with the whole TB already credited at its start,
  a mid-TB MMIO callback no longer needs the boundary clock move; keep
  only the virtual-timer sync (wasm_io_advance(0)) when the access
  crossed a timer deadline.  The per-access tcg_tb_lookup() +
  insn_start unwind of the old wasm_io_account() is gone.  The stock
  cpu_io_recompile rewind stays for rom_device (flash commands).
- translate-all.c: the per-session MMIO accounting state machine of
  the reworked 0004 (wasm_io_account/reset/rest) is removed; with
  per-TB crediting it has nothing left to adjust.

Device-visible clock semantics change by at most one TB (typically a
few guest insns): an MMIO access mid-TB now sees a clock that already
includes the whole TB instead of the exact io-insn boundary.  Boot
verified: the S75 fullflash reaches the idle screen (wallpaper, clock,
"Поиск сети") with no >>EXIT<<, LCD updating.

Measured (S75 fullflash, headless Chromium, tools/serialwatch.mjs,
10 s WATCH samples; baseline = two runs of the 0001-0004+0006 build,
both within ±2% of each other):

  insns executed at fixed wall time   gain
  t=20 s    93M           -> 197M    +113%
  t=40 s    195M          -> 374M     +92%
  t=60 s    315M          -> 629M    +100%
  t=80 s    425M          -> 783M     +84%

  virtual time at t=60 s: 3.96 s -> 7.21 s (+82%)
  boot to idle screen:    ~260 s wall (baseline run never passed
                          v=32 s in 150 s; extrapolated ~2x faster)

Known accepted deviations (rare paths, measured harmless on the boot):
- goto_ptr-chained TBs (indirect branches) used to be uncounted; they
  are counted now (more accurate than before).
- the rom_device cpu_io_recompile rewind re-executes insns that the
  header already credited (over-counts the rewound prefix; flash
  commands are rare).

Conflicts with the 0005 wasm32 DRAFT (goto_tb/tci emitters); that
patch needs a rebase onto this per-TB header model.
---
Date: Mon, 8 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

diff --git a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c
--- a/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c	2026-09-08 00:22:21.519619531 +0000
+++ b/accel/tcg/cpu-exec.c	2026-09-08 00:04:59.395049597 +0000
@@ -441,39 +441,14 @@
 
 #ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
     /*
-     * icount2 cycle accounting is batched per TB on emscripten (the
-     * per-instruction helper would need a libffi/JS roundtrip per guest
-     * instruction under TCI; see target/arm/tcg/translate.c).
-     * Snapshot the count before executing: the TB may be invalidated
-     * (io recompile / self-modifying code) while tcg_qemu_tb_exec runs.
+     * icount2 accounting runs in the interpreter: every TB (this one
+     * and any goto_tb/goto_ptr-chained ones) starts with a tci_tbhdr
+     * op that advances the clock by the TB's guest-insn count
+     * (tcg/tci.c, tcg_out_tb_start).  Nothing to account here.
      */
-    unsigned tb_icount = itb->icount;
-    {
-        extern void wasm_io_account_reset(TranslationBlock *session_tb);
-        wasm_io_account_reset(itb);
-    }
 #endif
     qemu_thread_jit_execute();
     ret = tcg_qemu_tb_exec(cpu_env(cpu), tb_ptr);
-#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
-    if (icount2_enabled()) {
-        extern void wasm_tb_account(unsigned insns);
-        unsigned rest;
-        {
-            extern unsigned wasm_io_account_rest(unsigned tb_icount);
-            rest = wasm_io_account_rest(tb_icount);
-        }
-        wasm_tb_account(tb_icount);
-        /*
-         * Stock-equivalent credit: mid-TB io accesses were accounted
-         * at their own boundaries (each +1 like the stock 1-insn
-         * CF_MEMI_ONLY TB), the executed prefix of the aborted TB is
-         * lost, and only the insns after the last io are credited
-         * here (translate-all.c).
-         */
-        icount2_advance(rest);
-    }
-#endif
     cpu->neg.can_do_io = true;
     qemu_plugin_disable_mem_helpers(cpu);
     /*
diff --git a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c
--- a/accel/tcg/cputlb.c	2026-09-08 00:22:21.519680973 +0000
+++ b/accel/tcg/cputlb.c	2026-09-08 00:05:18.555582625 +0000
@@ -1291,17 +1291,16 @@
          * and an MMIO polling loop re-pays it on every iteration
          * forever (the unsplit TB stays cached).
          *
-         * This tree batches icount2 accounting once per TB after
-         * execution (see cpu_tb_exec), so instead of rewinding we
-         * credit the cycles of the insns that already executed in
-         * this TB right here (wasm_io_account, translate-all.c): the
-         * callback then sees the clock at the io insn boundary, and
-         * the post-TB accounting adds only the remainder.  Skipping
-         * the rewind outright (as an earlier dropped patch did)
-         * leaves the clock frozen at the TB start - the boot-ROM GPTU
-         * SRC7 poll at 0x400118c then reads a timer armed earlier in
-         * the same TB as never elapsed and the boot aborts (FILE:
-         * flash ExitCode 0x0552, doc/early-crash-postmortem.md).
+         * With TB chaining the clock is advanced per TB by the
+         * tci_tbhdr header op (tcg/tci.c), so the callback already
+         * sees a clock that includes this TB - skipping the rewind
+         * changes nothing about clock visibility.  The earlier
+         * batched-after-TB accounting (patches 0002/0004 era) needed
+         * the boundary move here; a dropped patch that skipped it
+         * entirely left the GPTU SRC7 poll at 0x400118c reading a
+         * timer armed earlier in the same TB as never elapsed and
+         * aborted the boot (FILE: flash 0x0552,
+         * doc/early-crash-postmortem.md).
          */
         static bool rewind_mode, rewind_mode_init;
         if (unlikely(!rewind_mode_init)) {
@@ -1318,8 +1317,14 @@
          */
         if (icount2_enabled() && !rewind_mode &&
             !section->mr->rom_device) {
-            extern void wasm_io_account(CPUState *cpu, uintptr_t retaddr);
-            wasm_io_account(cpu, retaddr);
+            /*
+             * The chained-TB clock is already at/after this access
+             * (tci_tbhdr credited the whole TB at its start); just run
+             * any virtual timers whose deadline it crossed so the
+             * callback sees their effects (system/icount2.c).
+             */
+            extern void wasm_io_advance(unsigned cycles);
+            wasm_io_advance(0);
         } else {
             cpu_io_recompile(cpu, retaddr);
         }
diff --git a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
--- a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c	2026-09-08 00:22:21.519741535 +0000
+++ b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c	2026-09-08 00:05:10.107211308 +0000
@@ -174,108 +174,14 @@
 /*
  * wasm: mid-TB MMIO clock accounting (see io_prepare(), cputlb.c).
  *
- * icount2 cycles are batched per TB on emscripten (patch 0002): the
- * whole TB's icount is credited only after tcg_qemu_tb_exec() returns,
- * so a device callback for an access in the middle of a TB would see
- * the virtual clock frozen at the TB start.  Stock qemu avoids that by
- * rewinding the TB (cpu_io_recompile), whose cpu_loop_exit() longjmp
- * costs ~150us under emscripten and is re-paid on every pass of an
- * MMIO polling loop (16k recompiles / 20s across 229 TBs here).
- *
- * We skip the rewind but reproduce its icount2 clock exactly:
- *
- *  - At the access, wasm_io_account() moves the clock to T0 + (k - 1)
- *    for the k-th io access of the TB (T0 = ticks at TB start): the
- *    stock callback sees the TB-boundary clock for the first access
- *    and, for later ones, +1 per earlier io insn (each re-executed as
- *    a 1-insn CF_MEMI_ONLY TB).  The io insn index comes from the same
- *    insn_start unwind cpu_io_recompile uses.
- *
- *  - At TB end, cpu_tb_exec() credits wasm_io_account_rest(): the
- *    executed prefix of the (stock-aborted) TB is lost, each io insn
- *    counts +1, and only the insns after the last io run as normal
- *    follow-up TBs - exactly the stock per-TB accounting, including
- *    its lost-partial-TB cycles the firmware timing is tuned to.
- *
- *  - An access from a TB chained via helper_lookup_tb_ptr() (indirect
- *    branches; the interpreter does not return to cpu_tb_exec between
- *    them) is credited +1 and loses the whole session prefix, as the
- *    stock rewind - which unwinds the entire chain - would.
- *
- * Only the vCPU thread touches this state (translation and execution
- * both run there); no locking needed.
+ * With TB chaining (tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc) the icount2 clock is
+ * advanced by the tci_tbhdr op at every TB entry, so the whole TB is
+ * already credited when a device callback runs mid-TB - the callback
+ * sees the clock at most one TB (typically a few guest insns) ahead
+ * of the access.  All that remains to do here is run virtual timers
+ * whose deadline the access may have crossed (wasm_io_advance(0),
+ * system/icount2.c) so the callback observes their effects.
  */
-static __thread unsigned wasm_io_n;          /* io accesses in this session */
-static __thread int wasm_io_idx_last;        /* insn index of last io, -1 */
-static __thread bool wasm_io_chained;        /* io hit a chained TB */
-static __thread int64_t wasm_io_t0;          /* ticks at TB start */
-static __thread TranslationBlock *wasm_io_session_tb;
-
-void wasm_io_account_reset(TranslationBlock *session_tb)
-{
-    wasm_io_n = 0;
-    wasm_io_idx_last = -1;
-    wasm_io_chained = false;
-    wasm_io_session_tb = session_tb;
-}
-
-unsigned wasm_io_account_rest(unsigned tb_icount)
-{
-    /*
-     * Stock per-TB accounting after the session: the executed prefix
-     * of a rewound TB is lost, each io insn is re-executed as a 1-insn
-     * CF_MEMI_ONLY TB (+1 each) and only the insns after the last io
-     * run as normal follow-up TBs.  Emulate exactly that loss.
-     */
-    if (wasm_io_chained) {
-        return 0;   /* the whole chain prefix is lost by the rewind */
-    }
-    if (wasm_io_n == 0) {
-        return tb_icount;
-    }
-    return wasm_io_n + (tb_icount - 1 - (unsigned)wasm_io_idx_last);
-}
-
-void wasm_io_account(CPUState *cpu, uintptr_t retaddr)
-{
-    TranslationBlock *tb = tcg_tb_lookup(retaddr);
-    uint64_t data[INSN_START_WORDS];
-    int insns_left;
-    extern int64_t icount2_ticks_now(void);
-    extern void wasm_io_advance(unsigned cycles);
-
-    if (tb != wasm_io_session_tb) {
-        /*
-         * Chained via helper_lookup_tb_ptr(): the stock rewind would
-         * longjmp out of the whole chain (losing it) and re-execute
-         * this access as a 1-insn TB: give it its +1.
-         */
-        wasm_io_chained = true;
-        wasm_io_advance(1);
-        return;
-    }
-    insns_left = cpu_unwind_data_from_tb(tb, retaddr, data);
-    if (insns_left < 0) {
-        return;
-    }
-
-    wasm_io_idx_last = (int)tb->icount - insns_left;
-
-    /*
-     * The k-th io access of the TB must see the clock the stock path
-     * shows it: T0 + (k - 1) - the aborted TB is never credited, each
-     * earlier io insn's 1-insn TB is.
-     */
-    if (wasm_io_n == 0) {
-        wasm_io_t0 = icount2_ticks_now();
-    }
-    wasm_io_n++;
-    int64_t want = wasm_io_t0 + (wasm_io_n - 1);
-    int64_t now = icount2_ticks_now();
-    if (want > now) {
-        wasm_io_advance((unsigned)(want - now));
-    }
-}
 #endif
 
 /*
diff --git a/tcg/tci.c b/tcg/tci.c
--- a/tcg/tci.c	2026-09-08 00:22:21.515196789 +0000
+++ b/tcg/tci.c	2026-09-08 00:04:40.520524622 +0000
@@ -1174,6 +1174,26 @@
             }
             break;
 
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+        case INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr:
+            /*
+             * TB header (emitted by tcg_out_tb_start): advance the
+             * icount2 clock by this TB's guest-insn count.  Executed at
+             * every TB entry, including goto_tb/goto_ptr chain targets,
+             * so TB chaining (see tcg_out_goto_tb) keeps the clock
+             * instruction-proportional.  cpu_tb_exec() no longer
+             * accounts executed TBs.
+             */
+            tci_args_ri(insn, &r0, &t1);
+            {
+                extern void wasm_tb_account(unsigned insns);
+                extern void icount2_advance(uint32_t cycles);
+                wasm_tb_account((unsigned)t1);
+                icount2_advance((uint32_t)t1);
+            }
+            break;
+#endif
+
         case INDEX_op_br:
             tci_args_l(insn, tb_ptr, &ptr);
             tb_ptr = ptr;
diff --git a/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc b/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc
--- a/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc	2026-09-08 00:22:21.220597406 +0000
+++ b/tcg/tci/tcg-target-opc.h.inc	2026-09-08 00:04:23.204043073 +0000
@@ -15,3 +15,9 @@
 DEF(tci_movcond32, 1, 2, 1, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
 DEF(tci_qemu_ld_rrr, 1, 2, 0, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
 DEF(tci_qemu_st_rrr, 0, 3, 0, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+/* wasm only: TB header carrying the guest-insn count, executed at every
+ * TB entry (cpu_tb_exec call, goto_tb chain jump, goto_ptr target) so the
+ * icount2 clock advances per executed TB even while TBs are chained. */
+DEF(tci_tbhdr, 0, 0, 1, TCG_OPF_NOT_PRESENT)
+#endif
diff --git a/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc b/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc
--- a/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc	2026-09-08 00:22:21.510383876 +0000
+++ b/tcg/tci/tcg-target.c.inc	2026-09-08 00:04:28.879200882 +0000
@@ -462,18 +462,6 @@
 
 static void tcg_out_goto_tb(TCGContext *s, int which)
 {
-#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
-    /*
-     * Terminate the TB instead of emitting a chain jump: on emscripten the
-     * icount2 accounting runs per executed TB in cpu_tb_exec(), so every TB
-     * boundary must return through cpu_exec.  Exit with the (tb | idx)
-     * encoding of tcg_gen_exit_tb, which lets the cpu loop keep chaining
-     * via tb_add_jump() with real TranslationBlock pointers.
-     */
-    tcg_out_exit_tb(s, (uintptr_t)s->gen_tb | which);
-    set_jmp_reset_offset(s, which);
-    return;
-#endif
     /* indirect jump method. */
     tcg_out_op_p(s, INDEX_op_goto_tb, (void *)get_jmp_target_addr(s, which));
     set_jmp_reset_offset(s, which);
@@ -1250,7 +1238,15 @@
 
 static void tcg_out_tb_start(TCGContext *s)
 {
-    /* nothing to do */
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    /*
+     * Emit the TB header (see INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr): the interpreter
+     * executes it at every TB entry and advances the icount2 clock by
+     * the TB's guest-insn count there.  This keeps the clock strictly
+     * instruction-proportional even when TBs are chained via goto_tb.
+     */
+    tcg_out_op_ri(s, INDEX_op_tci_tbhdr, 0, s->gen_tb->icount);
+#endif
 }
 
 bool tcg_target_has_memory_bswap(MemOp memop)
